---
name: beam-offer-federation
description: Build a virtual offer provider — a microservice implementing IFederatedVirtualOffer that resolves, delivers and undoes the offers Beamable grants — and use the player and operator offer routes.
---

# Virtual Offer Federation

> General microservice workflow: `beam-manage-service`. Bundling: `beam-bundles`. Granting offers from a campaign send node: `beam-campaign-api`. Calling the player routes from a web client: `beam-web-guide`.

## High-Level Architecture

```
Campaign send page / operator POST /offers/grant
        │  GrantMany: offer_grants rows written Pending (id = hash(cid, pid, origin, originKey, entryId))
        ▼
OfferService ──▶ GrantOffers(grants) ──▶ provider microservice: validate + resolve offer
        │                                   └─▶ OfferGrantResponse { offer, providerMetadata }
        ▼  message staged (campaign) / request answered (operator)
Confirm: Pending → Granted, providerMetadata stored; the snapshot once per realm (offer_snapshots)

Player ──▶ GET /api/offers ──▶ registry page (Granted/Claiming) ──▶ GetOffers(grants) per provider ──▶ availability
                                                               └─▶ campaign gate (stat rule) folded in
Player ──▶ POST /api/offers/redeem ──▶ claim (CAS; exclusive group anchor) ──▶ gate ──▶ RedeemOffer(grant, params)
                                         ◀── Settled → Redeemed (+ forfeits) · Refused → Granted · Ambiguous → stays Claiming

Version end / revoke-origin ──▶ ExpireOrigin: open grants of the origin closed (read as Expired)
```

